{"id": "en_lightning_hike_p2", "total": 66.63, "segments": [{"text": "Part two. Freezing rainwater floods Jake's rock overhang shelter as darkness sets in around him.", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.98}, {"text": "The rock shelter is not a real building, so Jake must keep moving down quickly.", "start": 5.4, "end": 9.0}, {"text": "No place outside is truly safe when thunder roars loudly across the high mountain.", "start": 9.96, "end": 13.46}, {"text": "Only a sturdy building or a hard-top car provides real protection from lightning strikes.", "start": 14.06, "end": 17.48}, {"text": "One. Get off peaks and high ridges immediately and head down to safer ground.", "start": 17.454, "end": 22.26}, {"text": "Jake leaves the flooded rock overhang and runs away down the steep mountain slope.", "start": 23.06, "end": 25.94}, {"text": "Two. Never shelter under a lone tree or stand near dangerous metal fences outside.", "start": 25.71, "end": 30.48}, {"text": "Jake avoids a lone tree and stays far away from a long metal fence.", "start": 31.28, "end": 33.92}, {"text": "Three. Spread a group out so 1 strike does not hit everyone at once.", "start": 33.71, "end": 37.86}, {"text": "Jake sees other hikers nearby and tells them to spread out along the trail.", "start": 38.68, "end": 41.26}, {"text": "They separate quickly so 1 lightning strike cannot hit all of them together.", "start": 41.68, "end": 44.3}, {"text": "Down the trail, Jake sees a parking area with a hard-top car parked safely.", "start": 45.2, "end": 48.26}, {"text": "He runs toward the hard-top car and opens the door to enter shelter immediately.", "start": 48.72, "end": 51.34}, {"text": "Inside the hard-top car, Jake is finally safe from the roaring mountain thunderstorm.", "start": 52.28, "end": 55.38}, {"text": "Remember, when thunder roars, go indoors because no place outside is ever safe.", "start": 55.94, "end": 59.84}, {"text": "Always seek a building or hard-top car. Follow for a new scenario tomorrow.", "start": 